	"description": [
		"This course provides a social science understanding of the \"contemporary American family\" and analysis of marriage and family issues from a cross-cultural perspective. Students discuss issues of dating and mate selection, marital and parent-child relationships over the family life cycle, gender issues, work and family roles and problem-related issues affecting families (divorce, violence and death) caused by rapid changes in society. Offered Fall and Spring Semester."
